From 82892344ed2e9a4991fbb504db9e48c8d972c85e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:40:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] rdna-boosts: block 08: fused kernels (old-08 fusions +
 old-13 fused MoE + old-15 PR57/63)

Merged from the planned 08 fused-prefill and 09 fused-moe: the two are not
hunk-separable (the fusions and the mmvq dispatch share ggml_cuda.cu try_fuse,
mmvq.cu, norm.cu, common.cuh and the ggml_cuda_mm_fusion_args plumbing), and the
old-08-only fusion set was not correct (fusion-on greedy text differed from
fusion-off).

Contents:
- old-08 fusions: gdn-conv, ple-conv, norm-gated, topk-moe, the norm/unary/
  getrows/argsort kernels, the CPU references and the try_fuse arms.
- old-13: fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ, the mmvq short-K item-split/ksplit, the
  routed-compact MMQ (mmq.cuh/mmq-config), MWR, the mmq gate instances.
- old-15 PR #57/#63: the mmvq multi-row/row-loop decode (GGML_MMVQ_RDNA4_
  DECODE_GRID, nrows_loop, the lf_nval halving reduction), ssm_gate_beta/
  ssm_conv_l2_gatebeta, the norm rms_norm_q8_1 refactor and quantize_mmq_q8_1_glu.

The MoE-cache-aware arms (moe_cache_get_cold/redirect, the B1 stand-down) and
the qwen4exp/HC arms are deliberately NOT here -- they belong to the slab-moe and
qwen4exp blocks, and their absence leaves the resident-only path (bit-identical).

Gates: build all OK; fusion on == off (4B greedy text); test-logits-width-probe
width_purity PASS; MUL_MAT 2444/2444.

Amended (r132): the Q8_1 quantize cache is keyed by the ROOT tensor's identity but filled from the (possibly
offset) view's pointer, so an offset view stored its rows under the root identity and a later op with the same
root and canonical row layout could hit them.  Every key walk that reaches the cache now stops at the first
pointer change (this block: the four mmvq sites and the unary mul_q8_1 site; block 10 adds its own GLU site), so
offset-free views keep the shared root entry and an offset view gets its own arena entry.  A new
q8_1_src_range_ok() validates the source read range against the root buffer's allocation before every
quantize_row_q8_1_cuda / fused gated-q8_1 launch, so a stale source pointer (a compute buffer reallocated under a
still-matching cache entry) aborts loudly with the layout logged instead of faulting with
HSA_STATUS_ERROR_MEMORY_APERTURE_VIOLATION or silently reading reused memory.

Reported in PR #218 (@slavap), whose V620 hit the fault on decode.  Not reachable on the maintainer's model set
(0 offset-view keys in 14336-60416 key walks per config across 7 configs, probed on gfx1201), so this is a
correctness fix for configurations we do not run: 12/12 same-seed configs byte-identical, MTP acceptance
identical (1859/3416, 1420/1710, 2171/2483, 372/375 on the four axes), prefill-logit KLD 0.000000.

Co-authored-by: Slava P. <slavap@users.noreply.github.com>

Amended (r161): the routed fused gate arm is back.  Upstream #29948's
`GGML_ASSERT(gate && !ids && ...)` in ggml_cuda_mul_mat_q is the *dense* arm's
precondition, but the ids path below dispatches this block's `has_gate` kernel
(ggml_cuda_mul_mat_q_switch_type_gate) over the routed weight tables, which is
exactly what the MoE gate/up+GLU prefill fusion calls with `ids != nullptr`, so
the assert aborted every config that reached it (issue #241: an lfm2moe server
prefill; reproduced on gfx1151 and on gfx1201 with GGML_PAIR_OFF=1).  `ids` is
no longer part of the assert -- bias/scale stay dense-only because the routed
arm sets none, and a routed call can never reach upstream's dense interleaved
kernel.  Gate: fused == unfused on the reporting MoE (byte-identical greedy
text; prefill-logit KLD -0.000000 / same-top-p 100.000 %).
